00:11:24.560 --> 00:11:25.080
Okay. Awesome.

238
00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:28.040
So some people have, so I'll give you a rundown on what agent skills are.

239
00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:31.360
So if normal documentation,

240
00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:34.760
markdown files that you have in your code base explain what something is.

241
00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:39.120
An agent skill is a way to explain how to do something step

242
00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:43.440
by step for the agent, so you can think of them as procedural guides

243
00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.640
that give you agent new capabilities

244
00:11:46.640 --> 00:11:51.440
and so one interesting thing that is unlocked with agent skills is that

245
00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:56.400
you also give the agent information on when to invoke that skill.

246
00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.640
Right? You don't just tell it what to do.

247
00:11:58.640 --> 00:12:00.520
You also tell it when it's applicable.

248
00:12:00.520 --> 00:12:03.800
And the agent can then figure out when you're doing something naturally

249
00:12:04.280 --> 00:12:06.480
that, hey, this skill is applicable to what we're doing

